WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:06.080
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie, this week on
Gotham Vigilantes are the coming for everyone

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:07.790
and it’s raining dead bodies.

00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:11.450
I don’t know about you guys, but Selina
Kyle and Gordon are my new favorite pairing

00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:13.879
next to Oswald and Gordon.

00:00:13.879 --> 00:00:23.490
They also just cast Nicholas D’Agosto as
Harvey Dent, which is very cool.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:26.750
So let’s do top 5 moments, then I’ll do
my review and some updates on Flash and Arrow

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:27.750
at the end.

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:30.560
Careful for spoilers from the episode if you
haven’t seen it yet, I’ll wait just a

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:32.670
sec...okay, here we go

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:35.489
Number 5 - Meet Sal Maroni, one of Gotham’s
Bigger Mobsters

00:00:35.489 --> 00:00:38.470
This is the character that Eric Roberts played
in The Dark Knight.

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:44.520
So based on the timeline, we can guess he’ll
only be getting worse from here on out.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:49.250
He’s being played by David Zayas from Dexter
on Gotham.

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:56.149
It’s fun to watch him being evil.

00:00:56.149 --> 00:01:02.000
They’re setting up a big confrontation between
him and Falcone.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.670
I loved the Emperor’s New Clothes reference.

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:07.930
In the episode he said “The Emperor has
no clothes” but you get the idea.

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:11.360
He’s just calling Falcone out as a fool
who can’t see what’s really going on around

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:12.360
him.

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:16.479
At least Maroni believes that, Falcone is
pretty shrewd, so I don’t think Fish Mooney

00:01:16.479 --> 00:01:26.110
or any of the other big mob characters will
be able to just dump him in 

00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:30.160
the bay.

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:33.549
Number 4 - Bruce and Alfred Start To Have
Some Fun

00:01:33.549 --> 00:01:36.409
I was glad they finally let the characters
loosen up a little.

00:01:36.409 --> 00:01:41.540
Yes Bruce Wayne is a dark character, but that
doesn’t mean he can’t have fun.

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:50.790
He’s still a little kid.

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:54.500
Batman mostly does a lot of punching, but
he does swordfight when he’s fighting villains

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:58.090
that primarily use swords like Ra’s Al Ghul.

00:01:58.090 --> 00:02:02.680
It wasn’t subtle at all either, but they
just want use to watch Bruce stuck on the

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:08.460
idea of protecting Gotham...without turning
into a criminal yourself in the process.

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:13.850
We’re only a few episodes into the first
season, so they have to directly set up a

00:02:13.850 --> 00:02:15.050
lot of big things like this.

00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:19.640
What I’m really hoping to see is an episode
where Bruce actually goes out and tries to

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:23.140
help someone, like if sees someone in trouble
while he’s out in public.

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:24.410
Or see him try to deal with a bully.

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:28.380
Just an instance of him toying with the idea
of piecing together clues and taking action

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:29.380
to solve it.

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:33.670
The Detective bit was a nice nod to Batman
being the World’s Greatest Detective.

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:35.610
Number 3 - The Penguin is on the Rise

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:40.220
I think the speed with which they brought
him back into the city tells you how important

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:42.270
his character is to season 1.

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:45.790
I like that they gave him the tuxedo looking
suit at the end.

00:02:45.790 --> 00:02:50.880
It’s all setup for Gordon and Penguin teaming
up to deal with the storm brewing on the Penguin’s

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:51.880
map.

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:55.870
This doesn’t really address the Arkham situation
that much, but that will also be a big part

00:02:55.870 --> 00:03:00.260
of this map here soon in the middle.

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:04.980
In the comics, Maroni actually funded Hugo
Strange’s expirements at Arkham Asylum on

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:06.620
the orders of Falcone.

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:10.410
I don’t know that the show will go in that
direction, but Hugo Strange will be part of

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:11.970
the Arkham storyline this season.

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:20.350
Oswald is just going to be like the evil medium
for Gordon that will help him see these connections.

00:03:20.350 --> 00:03:24.570
The implication being that Gordon dealing
with these bigger fish will leave room for

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:26.880
Oswald to move in on their territory.

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:30.020
Number 2 - Catwoman and Gordon are on the
case

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:34.340
Definitely my favorite pairing in the episode,
Selina Kyle montages have been the most fun

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:35.340
so far.

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:38.800
Did you notice how they’re letting her give
people the Batman Slip, like she’ll just

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:41.320
appear and disappear as she pleases.

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:43.880
Their field trip was just a continuation of
the Wayne killing.

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:48.191
I know based on the shiny shoes and the way
the story is positioning people there are

00:03:48.191 --> 00:03:51.570
a lot of theories about The Penguin being
the one to murder them.

00:03:51.570 --> 00:03:55.700
It’s true in the comics, Joe Chill is the
killer, but the show might be doing something

00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:56.700
different.

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:57.700
It could be merging those characters.

00:03:57.700 --> 00:04:01.850
It’s just that Joe Chill did not wear shiny
shoes in the comics, like he wasn’t a slick

00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:02.850
person.

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:04.490
He was just an alcoholic looking for booze
money.

00:04:04.490 --> 00:04:08.480
On Gotham, they’re making it seem like someone
with a special attention to style did it,

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:13.140
like say, someone who wears fancy suits and
would be crazy enough to murder the Waynes.

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:14.730
Just something to think about.

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:18.450
Plus I like the implication that the Penguin
will help Gordon put all these huge villains

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:23.220
behind bars, but then Gordon will realize
that his biggest ally is also the person behind

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:26.160
the huge season 1 mystery murder.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:29.390
Number 1 - Vigilante’s Are On The Rise

00:04:29.390 --> 00:04:34.540
More will be coming is probably a phrase they’ll
put on a poster.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:36.640
It’s also foreshadowing for the rest of
the season.

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:38.360
There will be more vigilantes, mostly violent
ones.

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:41.510
I’m hoping we get a Red Hood easter egg
at some point.

00:04:41.510 --> 00:04:43.180
There are a lot of negative Batman vigilantes.

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:45.170
Like flat out crazy ones.

00:04:45.170 --> 00:04:51.940
But supposedly the show has cast Sara Paxton
as Bette Kane, one of the characters to take

00:04:51.940 --> 00:04:54.730
on the mantle of Bat Girl in the comics.

00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:58.950
She used to be listed on the show’s IMDB
page, but she’s not there anymore, so it’s

00:04:58.950 --> 00:05:02.370
possible they cut her out of the pilot or
they’re not doing her character anymore.

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:06.620
But I do think the show will bring on actual
Batman Vigilante characters from the comics

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:07.620
this season.

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:10.650
Just people that Bruce Wayne can point to
as inspiration for better or worse.

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:16.850
For the most part, Gordon is really the only
good vigilante type person on the show for

00:05:16.850 --> 00:05:17.850
now.

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:20.690
He’s supposed to be the benchmark for hero.

00:05:20.690 --> 00:05:24.900
Let me know, what was your favorite moment
and which vigilante’s do you want to see

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:26.690
on the show next?

00:05:26.690 --> 00:05:29.500
There was the whole Barbara Kean Montoya Drug
Storyline.

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:32.370
I’m not sure what they’re doing with those
characters.

00:05:32.370 --> 00:05:36.930
I ended up giving the episode a B overall,
just because I feel like the ending completely

00:05:36.930 --> 00:05:39.020
threw away the Montoya scene.

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:44.180
That was all about creating a wedge between
Gordon and Barbara, but then Barbara totally

00:05:44.180 --> 00:05:47.750
buys Gordon’s explanation.

00:05:47.750 --> 00:05:54.220
No he would never kill someone, and to pour
salt in Montoya’s wound, the Penguin walks

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:56.250
through the door, looking like a million bucks.

00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:59.010
That’s about as far from dead as you can
get.

00:05:59.010 --> 00:06:06.760
So my big question is what the heck are they
trying to do with Montoya?

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:10.490
It feels like they were trying to give some
more dimension to the Barbara Kean character

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:15.160
by making her a former drug addict and bisexual,
but they completely undercut it at the end.

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:19.550
So I’m a little confused as to where both
those female characters are going.

00:06:19.550 --> 00:06:24.990
My favorite performance in the episode was
Camren Bicondova again, I feel like this is

00:06:24.990 --> 00:06:28.020
a show that wants you to know it’s a comic
book Dick Tracy looking show.

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:29.460
Like this is a Dick Tracy type environment,
so the characters are supposed to act in a

00:06:29.460 --> 00:06:30.460
comic book-y way.

00:06:30.460 --> 00:06:32.280
And Camren is just having fun with it, like
she should.

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:37.430
Some of the other actors look like they’re
taking it a little seriously like Ben McKenzie.

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:49.390
So I’d like to see him have a little more
fun with it.

00:06:49.390 --> 00:06:56.590
The Bullock Gordon montage was pretty awful,
I like montage storytelling, but the music

00:06:56.590 --> 00:07:02.900
they used felt very out of place and I just
wasn’t buying it.

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:09.890
So only big issues were the montage and Montoya
with Barbara, otherwise, very fun episode.

00:07:09.890 --> 00:07:12.760
Next up this week is The Flash, episode 1
is airing tomorrow.

00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:16.740
I’m going to try and get a few more bonus
videos out before then.

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:19.110
Arrow episode 1 is on wednesday.

00:07:19.110 --> 00:07:25.570
I’m probably going to combine my Q&amp;As for
those shows.

00:07:25.570 --> 00:07:30.380
I won’t be doing a Gotham Q&amp;A tomorrow just
because of all that stuff, but there will

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:31.990
be extra flash and arrow videos.

